Description: Install Athena archive keyring before apt-cdrom add
 Athena ships a project signing key (Athena Build <athena@local>) and
 signs dists/<suite>/Release with it (Release.gpg + InRelease).  The
 matching pubkey rides on the disc at /cdrom/.disk/archive-key.gpg
 (placed there by scripts/iso_installer.py:_export_pubkey_to_staging).
 .
 For apt-cdrom add inside the target chroot to accept the signed
 Release, the pubkey must already be in /target/etc/apt/trusted.gpg.d/
 — apt-cdrom verifies signatures using the keyring as it exists at the
 moment of the call, not via any later step.  This patch inserts that
 install step into base-installer's configure_apt, between the
 00NoMountCDROM apt-config write and the apt-cdrom add invocation.
 .
 Without this patch: apt-cdrom add still appears to succeed at writing
 sources.list, but apt-setup's later verification step runs apt-get
 update which gets "NO_PUBKEY" → "does not have a Release file" → rc=100
 → apt-setup discards 40cdrom's output → final /target/etc/apt/sources.list
 has no cdrom entry → post-install apt-get install <pkg> fails with
 "Unable to locate package".  Diagnosed end-to-end 2026-05-13 via a
 local apt-cdrom repro under /tmp/apt-cdrom-repro/ — see Phase C
 diagnosis in docs/known-issues.md.
 .
 Guard with `[ -f /cdrom/.disk/archive-key.gpg ]` so the patch is a
 no-op on stock Debian discs (which use the debian-archive-keyring
 deb baked into the base set instead).  This means we can drop our
 patched base-installer onto a stock disc without breaking it.
Author: Harkirat S Virk <harkiratsvirk@gmail.com>
Origin: local
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-05-13
---
This patch header follows DEP-3: http://dep.debian.net/deps/dep3/
--- a/library.sh
+++ b/library.sh
@@ -872,6 +872,16 @@ configure_apt () {
 }
 EOT

+		# Install Athena archive keyring so apt-cdrom can verify our
+		# signed Release.  Without this the apt-cdrom add below
+		# appears to succeed but the later apt-setup verify step
+		# fails with NO_PUBKEY → "does not have a Release file".
+		if [ -f /cdrom/.disk/archive-key.gpg ]; then
+			mkdir -p /target/etc/apt/trusted.gpg.d
+			cp /cdrom/.disk/archive-key.gpg \
+			   /target/etc/apt/trusted.gpg.d/athena-archive-keyring.gpg
+		fi
+
 		# Scan CD-ROM or CD image; start with clean sources.list
 		# Prevent apt-cdrom from prompting
 		: > $APT_SOURCES
